winch secret generate: write a random password as a secret

Examples:
  # write a password into the vars of the group all
  winch secret generate vars.monit_password
  # write a password into the vars of one host
  winch secret generate vars.db_password --host db1.acme.com
  # write a password into the inventory production
  winch secret generate vars.db_password --inventory production

Usage:
  winch secret generate vars.<name> [flags]

Generate makes a random password of 32 letters and digits, encrypts it
for the recipients in winch.yaml, and writes it as a !secret value into
the inventory.

It writes into the vars of the group all, or of the host of --host. The
file keeps its comments and layout.

Something in the project must read the variable. The variable must not
be in those vars yet, also not as null.

Flags:
  --inventory <name>          inventory to write
                              default: inventory in winch.yaml
  --host <name>               host whose vars get the value
                              default: the group all

See: winch doc secrets
